{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"compacted_at":1787257051558049001,"compiled_state":{"alias":"crusty-brinish-ass","assignee":null,"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","authorship":{"signed":2,"unsigned":0},"authorship_ledger":[{"content_hash":"4f5209bbf3eb5770084816c15671b65fd620f21d34de7023d123c043ca248ff7","event_uuid":"662a7a0c-093a-441c-9446-df787664ec30","position":{"commit_sha":"eb09adf017c71a6d3c11bcef1b87d1f76ca6a5f1","position":"1787254294337250001-662a7a0c-093a-441c-9446-df787664ec30"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"b651b6294d56a6e6a2d560034d3768144004750a0975de47bef4f7a2f6b57208","event_uuid":"a7575743-3e5b-4bb8-9aed-8015529bc030","position":{"commit_sha":"248dff74e4085ad3d537f9d955fe856e2f852b2b","position":"1787254321492835001-a7575743-3e5b-4bb8-9aed-8015529bc030"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1787254294337250001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"a7575743-3e5b-4bb8-9aed-8015529bc030","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"aa7b-5e47-6d3d-4615"}],"description":"## Summary\n\n`adapters/jira/acli_cli_ops.add_comment` is the only `--json` consumer in that module that\nreturns raw `json.loads(result.stdout)` straight to its caller. Every sibling normalizes or\nverifies the payload first:\n\n- `get_comments` -> `_parse_paginated_comments`\n- `_parse_acli_comments` (normalizes bare list / wrapped dict / unrecognised shape)\n- `get_issue` (unwraps `issues[0]`, raises when absent)\n- `create_issue` -> `_verify_created_issue` (raises loudly when no key)\n\nBecause `add_comment` skips that idiom, it hands its caller ACLI's **batch mutation envelope**\n(`{\"results\": [...], \"totalCount\": N, \"successCount\": N}`) while its declared type\n(`_backend.py`: `add_comment(...) -> dict[str, Any]`) and every consumer treat it as a created\n**comment resource**. That gap is exactly what let bug `irongrey-chubby-oxpecker`\n(`aa7b-5e47-6d3d-4615`) ship: `_record_comment_id` read `result[\"id\"]`, got `None` on every\nCloud post, and silently no-opped — leaving the dedup map empty and re-posting ~205 comments an\nhour until REB-1861 hit Jira's 5000-comment cap.\n\nThe compounding factor: **no recorded real ACLI payload exists anywhere in the repo.** Every\ntest double hand-invents the shape it wishes the CLI returned —\n`tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/apply/test_comment_id_capture.py` (`MagicMock`, `{\"id\": \"10001\"}`)\nand even `test_acli_comment_adf_encode.py`, the one test that stubs actual acli stdout, invents\n`'{\"id\": \"10001\"}'`. So both transports passed every test while only one of them was correct,\nand nothing could have caught it.\n\n## Suggested work\n\n1. Make `add_comment` normalize/verify like its siblings, so the transport boundary either\n   honours the declared resource contract or fails loudly rather than returning a shape its\n   caller cannot use.\n2. Audit the remaining `--json` mutation wrappers for the same raw-passthrough pattern.\n3. Establish recorded real ACLI payload fixtures (at minimum for `comment create`, captured\n   from a live probe) so doubles assert against observed reality instead of assumption. Note a\n   safe capture route exists: `acli jira workitem comment create --key <NONEXISTENT> --json`\n   returns the genuine envelope without mutating anything.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] `add_comment`'s return either conforms to the declared contract or the mismatch is\n      surfaced as an error, not a silently-unusable dict.\n- [ ] At least one test asserts against a RECORDED real ACLI comment-create payload rather than\n      an invented one.\n- [ ] The remaining `acli_cli_ops` `--json` mutation wrappers are audited and the finding\n      recorded.\n\n## Notes\n\nDiscovered while root-causing `aa7b-5e47-6d3d-4615`; that bug's own fix is deliberately narrow\n(record the mapping regardless of whether an id came back) and does NOT close this seam.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":[],"ticket_id":"3235-8aaf-e288-48f2","ticket_type":"task","title":"ACLI add_comment returns the raw batch envelope, not a comment resource","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["662a7a0c-093a-441c-9446-df787664ec30","a7575743-3e5b-4bb8-9aed-8015529bc030"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1787257051558049001,"uuid":"af981240-db82-493d-afc9-d6c16bd0795a"}